(Similarly for destination.)
(Now we need to assign operator before lock. assign_operator_resource requires candidate_prepared and operator_available. So after candidate_prepared we can assign.)
(Thus order for each availability:)
(- attach_task_profile)
(- confirm_candidate_preparedness (now candidate_prepared true))
(- assign_operator_resource (links operator, makes operator unavailable))
(- activate_origin_node (or activate_destination_node) (requires candidate_prepared, candidate_task_profile_linked, node linking, not node_ready, not node_occupied))
(- lock_origin_availability (requires candidate_prepared, candidate_operator_linked, origin_availability_node_linked, origin_node_ready, not origin_availability_locked))
(- (optional) release_operator_resource (makes operator available again, unlinks))
