(Thus we can achieve origin goals via load then unload, without lock or operator assignment. Similarly for destination: load_destination_payload then unload_destination_payload yields destination_availability_locked true, destination_availability_confirmed true, destination_node_occupied true, destination_node_ready true, cargo available, destination_payload_linked false.)
(Thus we don't need operator assignment or lock actions. That simplifies.)
(Now we need to ensure origin_node_ready and destination_node_ready before assembling transport leg (assemble_transport_leg requires origin_node_ready and destination_node_ready). After unload, nodes are ready. Good.)
